| **[forge9](https://github.com/nineforge0/forge9)**&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/nineforge0/forge9/stargazers"><img src="https://img.shields.io/github/stars/nineforge0/forge9?style=flat&label=&color=30363d&logo=data%3Aimage%2Fsvg%2Bxml%3Bbase64%2CPHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHZpZXdCb3g9Ii0xLjUgLTEuNSAyNyAyNyI%2BPHBhdGggZmlsbD0iI2ZmZiIgZD0iTTEyIDEuNmwzLjIgNi42IDcuMiAxLTUuMiA1LjEgMS4yIDcuMkwxMiAxOC4xbC02LjQgMy40IDEuMi03LjJMMS42IDkuMmw3LjItMXoiLz48L3N2Zz4%3D" alt="GitHub stars" height="24" align="texttop"></a><br><sub>Rust (`MIT`) · CLI, cross-platform</sub> | RPF9 command-line toolkit: decrypt the table of contents, list, search, extract, replace and repack with the table re-encrypted, plus `--verify` checks and hash-guarded patch mods ([forge9-mods](https://github.com/nineforge0/forge9-mods)). Cipher tables and key schedules are not shipped (you extract `tables.bin` and `keys.bin` from your own executable). `catalog` recovers entry names from TOC hashes; also parses PSIN/shaders/AWC, exports textured drawables to glTF (materials + BCPack), ships an LLVM-validated RDNA2 disassembler, and documents the container in [docs/rpf9_format.md](https://github.com/nineforge0/forge9/blob/main/docs/rpf9_format.md). Repacked archives are not yet shown loading in the game (a static read of the loader saw no signature enforcement, with virtual calls still unresolved). |
