## Console Translation Layers & Static Recompilation

Projects translating Xbox Series X|S (`Scarlett`) or PS5 system libraries, memory models, and RDNA2 shaders so console binaries can run natively on PC. The game's executable leaked on 2026-11-23 and the field has moved fast. Upstream `VIctory` now reaches the prologue with the picture fully drawn at about 1 fps, and its forks (next table) are where the speed is: they play the prologue and the next mission at roughly 5 to 20 fps on one machine each, with the best reporting sessions of 40 to 77 minutes. `xcl`, `five-star-recomp`, `PercyScarlett`, `OpenScarlett (CE)`, the Leonida continuations, `TuxBox` (Linux) and `g6shim` get through first-run screens, menus or the story intro. **Nothing is playable**: frame rates are single or low double digits, ray-traced lighting is missing or stubbed, and long runs still lose the GPU. Every number here is self-reported unless a tracker says it verified it. Take-Two has started filing takedowns: on 2026-11-24 GitHub disabled Leonida and its whole network of 3,007 forks, and several smaller repos have since disappeared without a public notice. macOS projects have [their own section](#macos).

| Project&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; | What it does and where it stands |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Leonida**&nbsp;<br><sub>`ItsNotRexed/Leonida` · taken down 2026-11-24 (DMCA)</sub> | **Taken down.** Was the scene's largest effort, a static recompilation project for build `1.0.2.1` with about 10,000 merged PRs. Its author stepped away on 2026-11-23 and took the repository and its Discord offline that night. The next day GitHub processed a [Take-Two DMCA notice](https://github.com/github/dmca/blob/master/2026/11/2026-11-24-take-two.md) against it and all 3,007 forks in its network. The code is GPL-3.0 and copies pushed as separate repositories are still up. **Reference copy:** [avivetech/Leonida](https://github.com/avivetech/Leonida) is the final upstream state with full history (11,521 commits, last commit `de4c373`, 2026-11-23 23:30 UTC, source only). **Continuations:** [ubiquitarianism/leonida](https://github.com/ubiquitarianism/leonida) has all of that plus 1,300+ new commits and boots through the launch movie, first-run UI and story load into the world phase on Windows and Linux/Proton, with no world frame verified yet. [leonida-ce](https://github.com/IAmNotSiob/leonida-ce) shows the game's own first-boot UI and legal pages, then loses the GPU device. [palmetto](https://github.com/luizwidmer/palmetto) executes draws and presents frames that are still black. [gta2pc](https://gitlab.com/BasGame1/gta2pc) is a continuation hosted on GitLab. All self-reported. These can vanish the same way. Lookalikes that offer a zip, an installer or a password are malware lures. |
| **[Xbox2Windows](https://github.com/R0Y00/Xbox2Windows)**&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/R0Y00/Xbox2Windows/stargazers"><img src="https://img.shields.io/github/stars/R0Y00/Xbox2Windows?style=flat&label=&color=30363d&logo=data%3Aimage%2Fsvg%2Bxml%3Bbase64%2CPHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHZpZXdCb3g9Ii0xLjUgLTEuNSAyNyAyNyI%2BPHBhdGggZmlsbD0iI2ZmZiIgZD0iTTEyIDEuNmwzLjIgNi42IDcuMiAxLTUuMiA1LjEgMS4yIDcuMkwxMiAxOC4xbC02LjQgMy40IDEuMi03LjJMMS42IDkuMmw3LjItMXoiLz48L3N2Zz4%3D" alt="GitHub stars" height="24" align="texttop"></a><br><sub>C++, Python (`MIT`) · Xbox Series → Windows</sub> | Static recompilation research: translates selected x64 code to C++ and gfx1013 shaders to desktop DXIL. Source-built programs run from entry to exit. With the leaked executable, a modified diagnostic build that skips assertions played the intro, showed readable setup text and reached loading on one laptop GPU; the unmodified executable, menu navigation and gameplay are unverified (tracking issue #870). |
| **[xcl](https://github.com/xcl-dev/xcl)**&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/xcl-dev/xcl/stargazers"><img src="https://img.shields.io/github/stars/xcl-dev/xcl?style=flat&label=&color=30363d&logo=data%3Aimage%2Fsvg%2Bxml%3Bbase64%2CPHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHZpZXdCb3g9Ii0xLjUgLTEuNSAyNyAyNyI%2BPHBhdGggZmlsbD0iI2ZmZiIgZD0iTTEyIDEuNmwzLjIgNi42IDcuMiAxLTUuMiA1LjEgMS4yIDcuMkwxMiAxOC4xbC02LjQgMy40IDEuMi03LjJMMS42IDkuMmw3LjItMXoiLz48L3N2Zz4%3D" alt="GitHub stars" height="24" align="texttop"></a><br><sub>Rust (`GPL-2.0`) · Xbox Series X\|S → Windows (D3D12)</sub> | Wine-style compatibility layer: game x64 code runs natively while XCL reimplements `kernelx`, `d3d12_xs`, DirectStorage, and XAudio2. All 26,698 programs in a RAGE 9 `shaders.rpf` translate. **Minecraft Preview and *Unicorn Overlord* are fully playable.** **GTA VI:** `main` starts in about 4 s, holds 30 fps through menus and settings (~15 GB RAM), and open NVIDIA branch [PR #2057](https://github.com/xcl-dev/xcl/pull/2057) reports entering an incomplete 3D world at about 5 fps on an RTX 5090 (short runs, self-reported). Run with `XCL_NETWORK=0`, because the crash reporter uploads a minidump on every crash. macOS forks are in the [macOS](#macos) section. |
