### VIctory forks

Most of the frame-rate work happens in forks of `VIctory`, usually stacked on `victory-fork` and tuned for one GPU. They trade fixes with each other quickly, so the numbers below change by the hour. All of them are self-reported from one machine unless noted, need tens of GB of RAM, and none is playable yet. Forks that have gone offline since (`ztrx`, `victory-perf`) are left out.

| Fork | Focus / Hardware | What it reports |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **[victory-fork](https://github.com/fxceless/victory-fork)**&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/fxceless/victory-fork/stargazers"><img src="https://img.shields.io/github/stars/fxceless/victory-fork?style=flat&label=&color=30363d&logo=data%3Aimage%2Fsvg%2Bxml%3Bbase64%2CPHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHZpZXdCb3g9Ii0xLjUgLTEuNSAyNyAyNyI%2BPHBhdGggZmlsbD0iI2ZmZiIgZD0iTTEyIDEuNmwzLjIgNi42IDcuMiAxLTUuMiA1LjEgMS4yIDcuMkwxMiAxOC4xbC02LjQgMy40IDEuMi03LjJMMS42IDkuMmw3LjItMXoiLz48L3N2Zz4%3D" alt="GitHub stars" height="24" align="texttop"></a> | Shared base for most forks; descriptor mirroring, water copy-back | Played from the opening through the prologue and past the first boat mission: 9 to 12 fps in rooms and light outdoor views, 5 to 6 fps in heavy ones. The GPU is lost after 30 to 50 minutes of play; shadowed areas are black. |
