macOS forks of `VIctory` and `xcl` are in the [macOS](#macos) section.

---

## macOS

Nothing here is playable on a Mac either, but several projects now run the Xbox Series build on Apple Silicon. Most take a Windows runtime (`VIctory`, `xcl` or a Leonida continuation) and run it under CrossOver or Wine, with Rosetta 2 for the game's x86-64 code and Apple's D3DMetal or MoltenVK for graphics. A few build a native Mac loader and Metal backend with no Wine at all; those have not drawn a game frame yet. Ordered by how far they get, all self-reported.

| Project | Kind | How it runs | Status |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **[VIctory-macOS](https://github.com/pragyaangaur/VIctory-macOS)**&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/pragyaangaur/VIctory-macOS/stargazers"><img src="https://img.shields.io/github/stars/pragyaangaur/VIctory-macOS?style=flat&label=&color=30363d&logo=data%3Aimage%2Fsvg%2Bxml%3Bbase64%2CPHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHZpZXdCb3g9Ii0xLjUgLTEuNSAyNyAyNyI%2BPHBhdGggZmlsbD0iI2ZmZiIgZD0iTTEyIDEuNmwzLjIgNi42IDcuMiAxLTUuMiA1LjEgMS4yIDcuMkwxMiAxOC4xbC02LjQgMy40IDEuMi03LjJMMS42IDkuMmw3LjItMXoiLz48L3N2Zz4%3D" alt="GitHub stars" height="24" align="texttop"></a> | `VIctory` port | CrossOver Wine built from source, D3DMetal (GPTK 4.0 beta 3), Rosetta 2 | **Furthest on a Mac.** The world loads and stays up on an M3 Max and an M5 Pro at 2.4 to 2.9 s per frame. On 2026-11-25 one M2 Pro tester reached the prologue's first gameplay prompt with the camera following input, at about 2 s per frame with broken lighting ([issue #50](https://github.com/pragyaangaur/VIctory-macOS/issues/50)). Its test suite passes on an M4. Open problems: Apple's shader compiler crashes on some world shaders, and Metal ends long submissions, after which the queue ignores work. About 30 outside contributors; no releases. |
| **[MetalVI](https://github.com/Aoody743/MetalVI)**&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/Aoody743/MetalVI/stargazers"><img src="https://img.shields.io/github/stars/Aoody743/MetalVI?style=flat&label=&color=30363d&logo=data%3Aimage%2Fsvg%2Bxml%3Bbase64%2CPHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHZpZXdCb3g9Ii0xLjUgLTEuNSAyNyAyNyI%2BPHBhdGggZmlsbD0iI2ZmZiIgZD0iTTEyIDEuNmwzLjIgNi42IDcuMiAxLTUuMiA1LjEgMS4yIDcuMkwxMiAxOC4xbC02LjQgMy40IDEuMi03LjJMMS42IDkuMmw3LjItMXoiLz48L3N2Zz4%3D" alt="GitHub stars" height="24" align="texttop"></a> | `VIctory` / `victory-fork` port | Wine-Proton, D3DMetal (GPTK 3), Rosetta 2 | Replaces write-watch fault tracking (unreliable under Wine on macOS) with hashed page diffs, caps placed textures and adds a shader pre-warm command. Enters the 3D world on an M1 Max at about 0.1 fps. |
| **[ScarlettMac](https://github.com/paveledits/ScarlettMac)**&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/paveledits/ScarlettMac/stargazers"><img src="https://img.shields.io/github/stars/paveledits/ScarlettMac?style=flat&label=&color=30363d&logo=data%3Aimage%2Fsvg%2Bxml%3Bbase64%2CPHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHZpZXdCb3g9Ii0xLjUgLTEuNSAyNyAyNyI%2BPHBhdGggZmlsbD0iI2ZmZiIgZD0iTTEyIDEuNmwzLjIgNi42IDcuMiAxLTUuMiA1LjEgMS4yIDcuMkwxMiAxOC4xbC02LjQgMy40IDEuMi03LjJMMS42IDkuMmw3LjItMXoiLz48L3N2Zz4%3D" alt="GitHub stars" height="24" align="texttop"></a> | `xcl` patch layer, plus a `VIctory-macOS` preview | CrossOver Preview, D3DMetal 4.0 beta 3, Rosetta 2 | XCL reaches the menus and world loading on an M3 Max. The 3D opening captures in its README come from the bundled `VIctory-macOS` preview build, below 1 fps with heavy artifacts. |
| **[MacBox](https://github.com/aykhanium/MacBox)**&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/aykhanium/MacBox/stargazers"><img src="https://img.shields.io/github/stars/aykhanium/MacBox?style=flat&label=&color=30363d&logo=data%3Aimage%2Fsvg%2Bxml%3Bbase64%2CPHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHZpZXdCb3g9Ii0xLjUgLTEuNSAyNyAyNyI%2BPHBhdGggZmlsbD0iI2ZmZiIgZD0iTTEyIDEuNmwzLjIgNi42IDcuMiAxLTUuMiA1LjEgMS4yIDcuMkwxMiAxOC4xbC02LjQgMy40IDEuMi03LjJMMS42IDkuMmw3LjItMXoiLz48L3N2Zz4%3D" alt="GitHub stars" height="24" align="texttop"></a> | `xcl` fork | CrossOver, D3DMetal, Rosetta 2 | Account picker, intro, legal screens and loading artwork on an M5 Max; the main menu is not reached. Those runs used a BCPack integration that is not in the published code. |
| **[xcl-mac](https://github.com/utkarshxdev/xcl-mac)**&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/utkarshxdev/xcl-mac/stargazers"><img src="https://img.shields.io/github/stars/utkarshxdev/xcl-mac?style=flat&label=&color=30363d&logo=data%3Aimage%2Fsvg%2Bxml%3Bbase64%2CPHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHZpZXdCb3g9Ii0xLjUgLTEuNSAyNyAyNyI%2BPHBhdGggZmlsbD0iI2ZmZiIgZD0iTTEyIDEuNmwzLjIgNi42IDcuMiAxLTUuMiA1LjEgMS4yIDcuMkwxMiAxOC4xbC02LjQgMy40IDEuMi03LjJMMS42IDkuMmw3LjItMXoiLz48L3N2Zz4%3D" alt="GitHub stars" height="24" align="texttop"></a> | `xcl` fork | CrossOver or Wine, D3DMetal, Rosetta 2 | Consolidates Apple Silicon patches and open upstream PRs (credited) and ships prebuilt `xcl.exe` test builds. No GTA VI world capture in the repo. |
| **[victory-mac](https://github.com/AeroUp/victory-mac)**&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/AeroUp/victory-mac/stargazers"><img src="https://img.shields.io/github/stars/AeroUp/victory-mac?style=flat&label=&color=30363d&logo=data%3Aimage%2Fsvg%2Bxml%3Bbase64%2CPHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHZpZXdCb3g9Ii0xLjUgLTEuNSAyNyAyNyI%2BPHBhdGggZmlsbD0iI2ZmZiIgZD0iTTEyIDEuNmwzLjIgNi42IDcuMiAxLTUuMiA1LjEgMS4yIDcuMkwxMiAxOC4xbC02LjQgMy40IDEuMi03LjJMMS42IDkuMmw3LjItMXoiLz48L3N2Zz4%3D" alt="GitHub stars" height="24" align="texttop"></a> | Leonida port (despite the name) | Wine 11, MoltenVK, Rosetta 2 | Ports the `ubiquitarianism/leonida` tree with a launcher, an upload ring for unified memory and workarounds for missing geometry shaders. Boots offline to the first-run controller screen on an M3 Pro; the 3D world needs 14,685 mesh pipelines that MoltenVK refuses. |
| **[XSXEmu](https://github.com/daeken/XSXEmu)**&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/daeken/XSXEmu/stargazers"><img src="https://img.shields.io/github/stars/daeken/XSXEmu?style=flat&label=&color=30363d&logo=data%3Aimage%2Fsvg%2Bxml%3Bbase64%2CPHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHZpZXdCb3g9Ii0xLjUgLTEuNSAyNyAyNyI%2BPHBhdGggZmlsbD0iI2ZmZiIgZD0iTTEyIDEuNmwzLjIgNi42IDcuMiAxLTUuMiA1LjEgMS4yIDcuMkwxMiAxOC4xbC02LjQgMy40IDEuMi03LjJMMS42IDkuMmw3LjItMXoiLz48L3N2Zz4%3D" alt="GitHub stars" height="24" align="texttop"></a> | Native loader, no Wine | Mach-O process under Rosetta 2; own GFX10 → Metal translator | Maps Xbox Series PE images itself, with an RPF9 shader-archive reader that takes its key context from your own executable (SHA-256 checked, no key committed). GTA VI code runs past CRT/TLS init, starts worker threads and reads real archives; no D3D12 device or frame yet. |
| **[Xenora](https://github.com/ranveersoni98/Xenora)**&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/ranveersoni98/Xenora/stargazers"><img src="https://img.shields.io/github/stars/ranveersoni98/Xenora?style=flat&label=&color=30363d&logo=data%3Aimage%2Fsvg%2Bxml%3Bbase64%2CPHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHZpZXdCb3g9Ii0xLjUgLTEuNSAyNyAyNyI%2BPHBhdGggZmlsbD0iI2ZmZiIgZD0iTTEyIDEuNmwzLjIgNi42IDcuMiAxLTUuMiA1LjEgMS4yIDcuMkwxMiAxOC4xbC02LjQgMy40IDEuMi03LjJMMS42IDkuMmw3LjItMXoiLz48L3N2Zz4%3D" alt="GitHub stars" height="24" align="texttop"></a> | Native emulator research | Own x86-64 guest path and Metal backend; no Wine, Rosetta or Vulkan | PE32+ loader, RDNA2 shader translator and Apple Metal backend in Rust. Runs synthetic guest programs and translated `gfx1030` shaders only; commercial games are unsupported. |

Smaller efforts worth watching: [rdna2-metal-lab](https://github.com/RiddleRailwayPowder/rdna2-metal-lab) (differential tests of translated RDNA2 shaders on Metal, plus a Rosetta SSE4a probe; one commit, no license yet), a native Metal backend for `VIctory` on the [`macos-offline-pe-inspection` branch](https://github.com/neko-no-otoko/VIctory/tree/macos-offline-pe-inspection) of `neko-no-otoko/VIctory` (synthetic tests only), and `ubiquitarianism/leonida`, whose tools and Vulkan GPU tests run on macOS through MoltenVK with Mac runtime PRs open. `MacBox` and `xcl-mac` start from the Mac branches of [Ahmet-Dedeler/xcl](https://github.com/Ahmet-Dedeler/xcl), which belongs to this list's maintainer.

**Tools that run on a Mac.** Release builds for macOS: [SixNG](https://github.com/holdmysocks/SixNG), [OpenVI](https://github.com/TheoBIET/OpenVI), [openrage](https://github.com/openragee/openrage), [forge9](https://github.com/nineforge0/forge9), [rpf9-explorer](https://github.com/breadbbbb/rpf9-explorer) (since `v1.4`) and [rdna2-dis](https://github.com/booomxd/rdna2-dis). Mac only: [6stars](https://github.com/meetox80/6stars) (Swift and Metal world renderer) and [bink-player-mac](https://github.com/Ahmet-Dedeler/bink-player-mac). Build on macOS from source: [Percy6Stars](https://github.com/Ahmet-Dedeler/Percy6Stars), [PercyStar](https://github.com/rpatty-dev/PercyStar) and [ttpf-viewer](https://github.com/paryzius/ttpf-viewer). The Rust and Python format tools (`bcpack-rs`, `bink2-decoder`, `rpf9-extract`, `gta6-explorer`, `ttpf-studio`, `rpf9-audio` and others) run anywhere. Windows only: `OpenSix`, `leonida-forge`, `SixFM`, `OpenRPF9`, `gta6-video-reader` and `BK2toMP4`.

---

## Format Documentation & Research

Byte-level specifications, field confidence tables, and reproducible inspection scripts reverse engineered from local file headers and decoded outputs.

| Project&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; | What it covers |
| :--- | :--- |
| **GTA6-Asset-Info**&nbsp;<br><sub>`TrinitronClient/GTA6-Asset-Info` · offline since 2026-11-25</sub> | **No longer public.** 19-part asset format spec maintained by the SixNG team (`RPF9`, texture dictionaries, `ttpf`, `BCPack` codec types, models, map data, materials, collision, navmesh, PSO schema, `AWC`/`ADAT` audio). The `TrinitronClient` org was deleted on 2026-11-25 (no DMCA notice on record). **Reference snapshot:** [Geeknasty/GTA6-Asset-Info](https://github.com/Geeknasty/GTA6-Asset-Info) holds the spec through PR #205 (`9f5bd4e`, 2026-11-25 04:15 UTC, GPL-3.0, docs and JSON only). |
