## Visualizers & Related Experiments

Standalone graphics, save, and media tools built alongside GTA VI / RPF9 format exploration.

- [Ahmet-Dedeler/weather-study](https://github.com/Ahmet-Dedeler/weather-study) (`TypeScript / WebGL2`) - Open-source WebGL2 weather engine and timecycle visualizer with volumetric clouds, ocean reflections, branching lightning, and 4K capture, inspired by RPF9 research.
- [Ahmet-Dedeler/bink-player-mac](https://github.com/Ahmet-Dedeler/bink-player-mac) (`Objective-C / macOS`) - Native macOS Bink2 (`.bk2`) video player, plus `tools/bk2mp4.sh` to convert `.bk2` to mp4 with video and all audio tracks using librempeg's open-source Bink 2 decoder (matched to RAD's output in [librempeg#217](https://github.com/librempeg/librempeg/pull/217) and [librempeg#218](https://github.com/librempeg/librempeg/pull/218), merged upstream), no RAD code.
- [LilBigJP/ztrx-ps5-save-import](https://github.com/LilBigJP/ztrx-ps5-save-import) (`Python, Rust / GPL-3.0`) - Converts decrypted PS5 GTA VI saves to load in the Xbox build under `ztrx` (note: includes an example decrypted PS5 save in `examples/`).
- [NotHGM/save-garage](https://github.com/NotHGM/save-garage) (`Python / GPL-3.0`) - Retail PS5 story-save editor (`v1.25.0`) documenting joaat-hashed stat tables: completion editor for 200 base vehicles, 102 tasks and gang operations, 23,760 searchable stats, 13 UI languages (built on [CoreyLyu76/gta6-save-editor](https://github.com/CoreyLyu76/gta6-save-editor); note: save decryption uploads your save file to `garlicsaves.com`).


**See also:** four trackers of the PC port efforts, which disagree mostly on scoring: on 2026-11-26 PortWatch and gta6-pc-race put `VIctory-7900XTX` first, Six on PC puts `klbf-lab` first and Does Leonida Boot ties `VIctory-Belobug-AMD`, `VIctory-7900XTX` and `klbf-lab`. [PortWatch VI](https://github.com/4lwayz/portwatch-vi) scores the leading runtimes on one ladder and tracks DMCA notices. [gta6-pc-race](https://github.com/vuyp/gta6-pc-race) ranks public builds on a 7-stage ladder with Picture, Speed and Stability lanes refreshed every ~15 minutes. [Six on PC](https://github.com/Github-Samuel/sixonpc) tracks efforts on one ladder with a lookalike-repo checker and hash lab. [Does Leonida Boot?](https://doesleonidaboot.com/race) refreshes every three minutes and follows the Leonida forks' boot chain in detail. All four rely on what the projects report. For reproducible cross-project hardware checks, [PortBridge](https://github.com/akimfomin/PortBridge) (`Python, C++ / MIT`) coordinates volunteer runs by hardware ([Test Lab](https://akimfomin.github.io/PortBridge/#/lab)), linking pinned source revisions to upstream GitHub threads alongside subgroup-lane and transfer-planner test harnesses.

---

## Format & Architecture Glossary

Quick reference for terms that show up across these repositories:

| Term | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- |
| `RPF9` | Rockstar Package File v9 (`9FPR` / `0x52504639`). Next-generation archive container used by GTA VI / RAGE 9, supporting nested RPFs, PSIN tables, and zlib/BCPack payloads. |
| `TTPF` | RAGE 9 texture store format holding mipmapped GPU-swizzled surfaces (`BC1`-`BC7`, `RGBA8`, `RGBA16F`, texture arrays, cubemaps). |
| `BCPack` | Block-compression stream format used on Xbox Series X\|S alongside GDeflate to compress GPU textures and resource pages. |
| `ADAT` / `AWC` | Rockstar audio bank containers storing multi-stream `Opus` and `XMA2` voice, SFX, and radio assets. |
| `BK2` (Bink 2) | RAD Game Tools video codec used in `movies.rpf` reels and UI cutscenes. |
| `RDNA2` (`GFX10.3`) | AMD GPU ISA used by Xbox Series X\|S and PS5. Tools like `xcl`, `VIctory` and `OpenScarlett` lift precompiled RDNA2 shader binaries to `SPIR-V` (Vulkan) or `DXIL` (D3D12). |
| `Scarlett` / `d3d12_xs` | Microsoft codename for Xbox Series X\|S and its console-extended Direct3D 12 + `kernelx` runtime shimmed on Windows by `OpenScarlett`, `xbox-emulator`, and `xcl`. |

---

## Safety & Scope

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Links and index only.** This list indexes GTA VI-related open-source tools, runtime layers, format documentation, and community resources. This repository hosts no game executables or build downloads; linked projects are maintained by their own authors.

> [!CAUTION]
> **There is no playable GTA VI for PC.** The game executable (`game_scarlett_master.exe`) leaked on 2026-11-23. Several open-source runtimes now start it, reach its menus and opening cutscene, and play the prologue and the first missions through `VIctory` forks at roughly 5 to 20 frames per second on one machine each, with missing ray-traced lighting and lost GPUs on long runs, but none is playable. This list does not link the executable. If you run it yourself, block its network access first: its crash reporter uploads a memory dump from your IP on every crash. Fake downloads and scam launchers are circulating too (including a public template that ships a self-signed `CN=Rockstar Games, Inc.` certificate with its private key, plus star-boosted companion-zip lures), so read the source and check what you run. For an example of how these fakes work, [Cyberleek-Gta6-Malware](https://github.com/Justyyin/Cyberleek-Gta6-Malware) is a write-up (with an English edition in `en/ANALYSIS.md`) of the October 2026 fake "Cyberleek Launcher" with defanged indicators and script text.

### Inclusion Criteria

Projects are checked before being added so the list stays useful and safe:

- **Included:** Helpful GTA VI-related projects with real code, libraries, runtime work, format research, or developer resources backed by actual commits.
- **Excluded:** Empty placeholder repos, leaked game executables or pirated build downloads, spam/clickbait/malware-bait repos (fake Switch/PS5 emulator farms, fake Rockstar-signed launchers, README-only repos with a release attached), and uncredited copies with no original work.

